WEBVTT

NOTE whisper small.en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:05.980
In the previous video, you saw how you can get a neural network to output four numbers,

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.780
Bx, By, Bh, and Bw to specify the bounding box of an object you want the neural network

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.180
to localize.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:18.860
In more general cases, you can have a neural network just output x and y coordinates of

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.820
important points in an image, sometimes called landmarks that you want the neural network

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.820
to recognize.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.820
Let me show you a few examples.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:31.460
Let's say you're building a face recognition application and for some reason you want the

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:37.140
algorithm to tell you where is the corner of someone's eye.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.860
So that point has an x and y coordinate.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:47.060
So you can just have a neural network, have this final layer, and have it just output two

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:54.100
more numbers, which I'm going to call Lx and Ly to just tell you the coordinates of that

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.780
corner of the person's eye.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:03.740
Now what if you wanted to tell you all four corners of the eye, really of both eyes.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.020
So if we call the points the first, second, third, and fourth points going from left to

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:16.020
right, then you can modify the neural network now to output L1x, L1y for the first point

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:25.220
and L2x, L2y for the second point and so on so that the neural network can output

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.700
the estimated position of all those four points of the person's face.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.580
But what if you don't want just those four points?

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:35.820
What do you want to output this point and this point and this point and this point, you know,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.380
along the eye, maybe output some key points along the mouth so you can extract the mouth

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.660
shape and tell the person is smiling or frowning, maybe extract a few key points along

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.580
the edges of the nose.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:53.860
But you could define some number for the sake of argument, let's say 64 points or

00:01:53.860 --> 00:02:00.860
64 landmarks on the face, maybe even some points, you know, that help you define the

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.140
edge of the face, defines the jawline.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:09.460
But by selecting a number of landmarks and generating a label training set that

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.900
contains all of these landmarks, you can then have the neural network tell you

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.020
where are all the key positions or the key landmarks on a face.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:25.340
So what you do is you have this image, now person's face as input, have it go through a

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:34.300
conf net and have a conf net then have some set of features, maybe have it output 0 or 1,

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:43.060
like is there a face in this or not, and then have it also output L1x, L1y and so on

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:48.740
down to L64x, L64y.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.260
And here I'm using L to stand for a landmark.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:03:02.700
So this example would have 129 output units, one for is there a face or not, and then if

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:09.580
you have 64 landmarks, that's 64x2, so 128 plus 1 output units.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.500
And this can tell you if there's a face as well as where all the key landmarks on the

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.740
face.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:21.660
So this is a basic building block for recognizing emotions from faces, and if you

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:27.140
played with the Snapchat and the other entertainment, you also AR augmented

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:32.220
reality filters, like the Snapchat filters can draw a crown on the face and

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.820
have other special effects.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:39.420
Being able to detect these landmarks on a face is also a key building block for

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:44.460
the computer graphics effects that warp the face or draw on various special effects

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.180
like put a crown or a hat on a person.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.260
Of course, in order to train a network like this, you will need a label training

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:58.820
set, we have a set of images as well as labels Y where people where someone will

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:05.860
have had to go through and laboriously annotate all of these landmarks.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:12.660
One last example, if you are interested in people post detection, you can also

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:19.500
define a few key positions like the midpoint of the chest, the left shoulder,

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:24.820
left elbow, the wrist and so on, and just have a neural network, you know,

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:31.660
sort of annotate key positions in the person's pose as well.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:36.740
And by having a neural network output all of those points I'm annotating,

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:42.740
you could also have the neural network output the pose of the person.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:48.580
And of course, to do that, you also need to specify these key landmarks,

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:56.980
like maybe L1X and L1Y is the midpoint of the chest down to maybe L32X, L32Y,

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.740
if you use 32 coordinates to specify the pose of the person.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:07.500
So this idea might seem quite simple of just adding a bunch of output units to output

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:12.780
the XY coordinates of different landmarks you want to recognize.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:18.060
To be clear, the identity of landmark one must be consistent across different images.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:22.580
Like maybe landmark one is always this corner of the eye, landmark two is always this corner

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.580
of the eye, landmark three, landmark four and so on.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.420
So the labels have to be consistent across different images.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:34.380
But if you can hire labelers or label yourself a big enough dataset to do this,

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:40.700
then a neural network can output all of these landmarks which you can use to carry out other

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:44.940
interesting effects such as estimate the pose of a person, maybe try to recognize

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:47.980
someone's emotion from a picture, and so on.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.380
So that's it for landmark detection.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:56.220
Next, let's take these building blocks and use it to start building up towards object detection.
